    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32550" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκπᾰθής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ʽπάθοσ̓</span>”
				<i>passionate, furious,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					16.23.5
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				15.3.4
			</span></i>, etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					1.7.8
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. πρός τι</span>
			<i>passionately eager</i> for a thing, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				1.1.6
			</span></i>, etc. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-θῶς</span> Teles<i><span class="en">
				p.35
			</span></i> H., <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				2.18.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>out of harm, unhurt,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Anon.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i></div>
